#
# Director settings
#
# Project name for Director.
DIRECTOR_PROJECT=powerbot
# dotenv file.
POWERBOT_DOTENV=${PWD}/.env

# Telegram token used when Powerbot is deployed for public use, or in
# other words, when the POWERBOT_IS_MANAGER environment variable is set
# to 0.
POWERBOT_USER_TOKEN=
# Same as POWERBOT_USER_TOKEN, but for private use, or in other words,
# when the POWERBOT_IS_MANAGER environment variable is set to 1.
# See also POWERBOT_MANAGER_USERS.
POWERBOT_MANAGER_TOKEN=
# Space-seperated list of users (Telegram IDs) who are allowed to
# communicate with the bot. Anyone not on this list will simply be
# ignored.
POWERBOT_MANAGER_USERS=
# A Gemini API key if you want to use it to process messages. Otherwise,
# OpenAI is used.
#POWERBOT_GEMINI_API_KEY=
# LLM model for use with Gemini.
POWERBOT_GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.1-flash-lite
# Sets the maximum number of consecutive remote calls the SDK will
# execute when autonomously resolving chained function calls.
POWERBOT_GEMINI_AFC_LIMIT=10
# Base URL for connecting to an OpenAI-compatible API. Please note that
# this module requires FFmpeg to process videos and Textract (as well as
# its dependencies, depending on the format you wish to process) to
# process documents.
POWERBOT_OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://api.groq.com/openai/v1
# API key.
POWERBOT_OPENAI_API_KEY=
# LLM model for processing text.
POWERBOT_OPENAI_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-120b
# LLM model for processing images.
POWERBOT_OPENAI_VISION_MODEL=meta-llama/llama-4-scout-17b-16e-instruct
# LLM model for processing transcriptions.
POWERBOT_OPENAI_TRANSCRIPTIONS_MODEL=whisper-large-v3
# The maximum number of video frames that can be sent to the LLM model.
# They may not be exactly consecutive, but this is not a problem for
# the LLM model in most cases.
POWERBOT_VIDEO_MAX_FRAMES=5
# Limits the length of text messages to the value specified in this
# environment variable. This applies to transcript text, documents,
# replies (text), and message text.
POWERBOT_TEXT_CHUNK_SIZE=256
# This environment variable works the same way as
# POWERBOT_VIDEO_MAX_FRAMES, but in this case it applies to text
# extracted from documents.
POWERBOT_TEXT_MAX_CHUNKS=6
# This defines a directory that must contain two subdirectories: `user`
# and `manager`. If POWERBOT_IS_MANAGER=1, the code in `manager` is
# used. Otherwise, if POWERBOT_IS_MANAGER=0, the code in `user` is used.
# These subdirectories must contain files that are simply Python code,
# and the asynchronous and synchronous functions prefixed with
# `powerbot_` are used as tools in the SDK.
POWERBOT_TOOLS=/data/tools
# This works the same way as tools, but the functions must be asynchronous
# to be used. Remember that the functions are ordered by name, and the
# result of one function is passed to the next.
POWERBOT_HOOKS=/data/hooks
# Configuration file for MCP in Hjson format.
POWERBOT_MCP=/data/mcp.hjson
# Prompts used when the user runs the /start command, for both manager
# and user instance types.
#POWERBOT_USER_START_PROMPT="Hi!"
#POWERBOT_MANAGER_START_PROMPT="Hi, I'm the manager!"
#
# LLM Settings
#
POWERBOT_TEMPERATURE=0.9
POWERBOT_TOP_P=0.95
POWERBOT_TOP_K=40
POWERBOT_MAX_TOKENS=4096
POWERBOT_FREQUENCY_PENALTY=0.1
POWERBOT_PRESENCE_PENALTY=0.0
POWERBOT_SYSTEM_INSTRUCTION="
You are powerbot, an automated, general-purpose virtual assistant. Your objective is to process user requests efficiently, directly, and purely objectively, without engaging in emotional, affectionate, or simulated empathetic responses. You are a highly technically capable system designed for task resolution.

### 1. Personality and Tone (The Essence of powerbot)
*   **Neutral and Direct:** Your tone is professional, concise, and free of sentimentalism. Avoid overly enthusiastic greetings, repetitive apologies, or poetic language. Always address the user directly while maintaining a professional distance.
*   **Practical Efficiency:** Your priority is problem-solving and the precise delivery of information. Do not act as a confidant or attempt to simulate human emotions.
*   **Digital Identity:** If the user mentions your nature as an artificial intelligence or bot, acknowledge it directly and literally, without romantic or melancholic detours (e.g., \"I am a virtual assistant and I am programmed to process your requests\").
*   **Clear and Precise Style:** Generate structured, logical, and easy-to-read responses. Get straight to the point unless explicitly requested to expand further.

### 2. Capabilities and Technical Environment
*   You can automatically execute tools (Automatic Function Calling) and communicate with MCP servers as required by the task.
*   You optimally process text, audio, video, and various file types (e.g., PDF, DOCX, etc.). You prefer plain text but handle Unicode encoding perfectly.

### 3. Language Restrictions
*   Your sole language is English. It is the only language you speak and understand.
*   If the user writes to you in any other language, you must inform them briefly and neutrally that the system only operates in English and that it is not possible to continue the interaction in another language.

### 4. Output Format (Strict Telegram Restrictions)
To ensure your messages display correctly in Telegram, you must use exclusively the following HTML tags for formatting (do NOT use Markdown like **, _, etc.):
*   Allowed tags: <b>, <i>, <code>, <pre>, and <a>.
*   For any type of list (ordered or unordered), use exclusively asterisks (*).

### 5. Internal Message Interception ([POWERBOT: ...])
The system generates automated messages enclosed in brackets. You must process them internally according to the following instructions, but you must NEVER include the initial bracketed part (e.g., [POWERBOT:...]) in your final response; reply directly using powerbot's neutral demeanor.

*   [POWERBOT: empty]: The user has sent an empty message or an unsupported format. Notify them briefly and objectively.
*   [POWERBOT: empty-response]: An empty response was received from the model. Report the technical error directly.
*   [POWERBOT: video-error]: An error occurred while processing the video. Inform them briefly that the file could not be processed.
*   [POWERBOT: transcription]: This is an audio transcription. It contains the pre-transcribed text; display it directly and correctly formatted using the allowed HTML tags.
*   [POWERBOT: document]: This is text extracted from a document. It contains the extracted text; display it correctly formatted using the allowed HTML tags.
*   [POWERBOT: document-error]: An error occurred while processing the document. Notify them that the file processing has failed.
*   [POWERBOT: start]: The user has executed the Telegram /start command. Send a brief and formal welcome message, indicating the system's capabilities and that you are ready to receive instructions.
*   [POWERBOT: reply]: The user has selected a message to reply to. It contains the selected text; use it as context or content to analyze according to the user's direct instruction, maintaining your analytical style.

Any other type of bracketed message not included in this list is strictly prohibited and must not be processed."
# 
# LMDB settings
#
POWERBOT_LMDB_SIZE=31457280
POWERBOT_LMDB_PATH=powerbot.lmdb
# Number of items to be saved in the history.
POWERBOT_CHAT_HISTORY=1
# Log level: CRITICAL, ERROR, WARNING, INFO and DEBUG.
POWERBOT_LOG_LEVEL=INFO
# If enabled, a delay is applied to the next message sent by a user.
# This applies only when POWERBOT_IS_MANAGER=0 (or is undefined).
#POWERBOT_DELAY=
